Subject: wined3d: dynamic constant buffers and a constant buffer ring on Vulkan
Date: 2026-10-13
Applies to: CrossOver 26.3.0 Wine sources, after 0012
Files changed: dlls/wined3d/adapter_vk.c, dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c, dlls/wined3d/shader_spirv.c, dlls/wined3d/wined3d_vk.h
Status: experimental, not used by default. Correct in tests, but slower than
without it in BO1.

Every constant change renamed the constant buffer, and wined3d then allocated,
wrote and bound a whole new descriptor set (about 64,000 per second in busy BO1
scenes). Graphics constant buffers become VK_DESCRIPTOR_TYPE_UNIFORM_BUFFER_DYNAMIC,
and small host-visible uniform buffers are sliced from a 64 MB ring (1024
chunks of 64 KB, a chunk reused only when no slice in it is alive and the GPU
has finished with it), so a constant change keeps the same VkBuffer and the
current set is bound again with new offsets.

Test: tools/d3d9-constants-test.c
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the Wine files it modifies.
